From 5395c24274eac28aaeb92c3e2d04804b3b39cd45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:55:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 65/74] Song browser: versions of a song grouped under its name

Files whose names begin with the same word (up to the first space, or the
extension; case doesn't matter) and sort next to each other ("TRACK",
"TRACK 2", "TRACK 3") are one row in the song browser: the group's first
version, shown by that word with an arrow (7-segment: "TRACK--"). Pressing
it (select encoder or LOAD) folds the group out and loads nothing; the
versions are shown indented and the select encoder goes through them;
pressing one loads it as before (also while playing, with the countdown).
BACK folds the group in (with none open it goes up a folder or exits as
before); scrolling out of the group folds it in; arriving on a later
version (the current song on entry, typing, a deleted file) folds its
group out. A song on its own looks and works as before; the save browser
is unchanged. Only a name continuing with '_' or '.', or a folder, can
sort between versions: the group is then two rows.

The encoder steps over a folded group's versions with
Browser::selectEncoderAction() without showing or previewing them, so the
window of file items is read again as before when a step leaves it; at
the window's edge the folder is read again around the selection, so a
row's group is known. The song browser keeps 100 file items instead of
20 (Browser::fileItemsWindow, the other browsers unchanged): the rows
around a folded group come from the window, and with 20 the row after a
group of more than about 8 versions was missing. A larger group works the
same; rows next to it are then filled from above.

